%K Wireless Sensor Networks; mean-field reinforcement learning; cooperative routing; energy efficiency; network lifetime
%X MeFi proposes a cooperative routing framework for large-scale WSNs using mean-field reinforcement learning to approximate multi-agent interactions, improving energy efficiency and balance while maintaining delivery performance to prolong network lifetime.

%0 Journal Article
%F Okine2024_TNSM
%M Okine2024_TNSM
%T Multi-Agent Deep Reinforcement Learning for Packet Routing in Tactical Mobile Sensor Networks
%J IEEE Transactions on Network and Service Management
%V 21
%N 2
%P 2155-2169
%D 2024
%U https://doi.org/10.1109/TNSM.2024.3352014
%A Okine, Andrews A.
%A Adam, Nadir
%A Naeem, Faisal
%A Kaddoum, Georges
%K Wireless Sensor Networks; tactical; jamming; multi-agent deep reinforcement learning; routing; multi-sink
%X Proposes a distributed MADRL-based routing scheme for multi-sink tactical mobile sensor networks under link-layer jamming; reward considers hop count to nearest sink, one-hop delay, next-hop PLR, and forwarding energy cost; outperforms baselines in PDR, latency, and energy efficiency.

%0 Journal Article
%F Kaur2021_JIOT
%T Energy-Efficient Intelligent Routing Scheme for IoT-Enabled WSNs
%J IEEE Internet of Things Journal
%V 8
%N 14
%P 11440-11449
%D 2021
%U https://doi.org/10.1109/JIOT.2021.9324772
%A Kaur, Gagandeep
%A Chanak, Prasenjit
%A Bhattacharya, Mahua
%K Wireless Sensor Networks; deep reinforcement learning; unequal clustering; IoT; energy efficiency; delay
%X A DRL-based intelligent routing approach with unequal clustering guided by current data load reduces delay and extends network lifetime; ns-3 experiments show gains in alive nodes, packet delivery, energy efficiency, and communication delay versus state-of-the-art.